  "goodToKnow": "Der Böller is a firecracker or banger. Setting off fireworks (böllern) is a big Silvester (New Year's Eve) tradition in Germany, and private fireworks may normally only be sold in the last few working days of the year. Each year there's debate about a Böllerverbot because of injuries, attacks on emergency workers, fine dust and stressed animals; many cities have Böllerverbotszonen. The plural is the same: die Böller."
